What this package contains
--------------------------

Only the plugin itself: the Python modules that define the Horus blocks, the
block and flow definitions, the configuration pages and the bundled example
data. Nothing is compiled, and no third-party software is included.

Two things are deliberately left out of this archive and are created on the
machine that installs it: the plugin's own ``deps/`` folder, which Horus
populates from the dependency list in ``plugin.meta``, and the ``config/``
folder, which holds paths specific to one machine.

What this package does NOT cover
--------------------------------

The plugin drives external tools that it does not ship and whose terms this
licence does not grant: ProteinMPNN, MMseqs2, Rosetta and PyRosetta, BioEmu,
MAFFT and CodonTransformer, together with the Python dependencies installed
from the list in ``plugin.meta`` and any model weights fetched at install time.

Each of those carries its own licence, and reviewing them is the responsibility
of whoever installs and runs this plugin. Rosetta and PyRosetta in particular
are free only for academic and non-commercial use and need a commercial licence
from the University of Washington otherwise. The installation documentation
sets out what is downloaded from where:

    https://bsc-cns-eapm.github.io/protein-set-selection-horus/installation.html
